<Base title="About Haul Numbers" description="Haul Numbers builds free, accurate calculators for owner-operator truck drivers, published by sahamo.">
  <h1>About Haul Numbers</h1>
  <p>Haul Numbers makes free calculators for owner-operator truck drivers and small fleets. Every formula is documented on its page so you can check the math, and all calculations run in your browser.</p>
  <p>Results are estimates based on the numbers you enter. They are not financial, tax or legal advice.</p>

  <h2>Who writes this</h2>
  <p>Haul Numbers is published by <strong>{PUBLISHER_BRAND}</strong>, which also runs Funding
  Numbers, Rental Numbers, Freelance Numbers, Debt Numbers and Settlement Numbers — each a
  focused set of calculators for one audience, not a single do-everything site.</p>
  <p><strong>{AUTHOR.name}</strong>, {AUTHOR.role.toLowerCase()}. {AUTHOR.bio}</p>

  <h2>How this site is edited</h2>
  <p>Every calculator's formula is documented on its own page. Guides that cite outside figures
  list their sources and the date they were last checked, shown at the top of the guide.</p>
  <p>Some guide drafts are prepared with AI assistance from official sources — never from memory —
  and every draft is reviewed, edited and approved by {AUTHOR.name} before it's published. A guide
  that used AI assistance says so, next to its sources.</p>
  <p>We rely first on primary sources: government agencies (the IRS, the SBA and others) and the
  regulations they publish. Where a primary source isn't available yet, we say so and use a
  reputable secondary one instead.</p>

  <h2>Independence and corrections</h2>
  <p>This site is funded by advertising. Advertisers have no influence over the calculators'
  formulas or a guide's content, and we don't accept payment to feature or rank any product.</p>
  <p>If something looks wrong, <a href="/contact/">tell us which page and what you expected</a> —
  we check it against the source and correct confirmed errors promptly.</p>
</Base>
